/**
 * The icon set.
 *
 * These are the Mayfair icons from the office's own asset package: Phosphor
 * Regular, one family, drawn on a 256 unit grid. Every one arrives as
 * `fill="currentColor"` with no hard-coded colour or size, which is why an
 * icon here follows the theme and dark mode without a second definition.
 *
 * They replaced a set drawn by hand at 24 units. Mixing the two would have
 * been worse than either on its own, so the whole set moved across at once and
 * a test now refuses any icon on a different grid.
 *
 * Rules for this file:
 *
 * - Icons are decorative. Every one is `aria-hidden`, and the thing next to it
 *   carries the readable name. An icon never carries meaning alone.
 * - The paths are inlined rather than read from disk. A listing screen draws
 *   dozens of icons, and that would be dozens of file reads per page.
 * - `render()` is the only way to draw one. An unknown name returns an empty
 *   string rather than a broken glyph or a PHP notice.
 *
 * Source: github.com/devkaushall/dev_vault - Stock Package/mayfair-icons
 * Family: Phosphor Regular, MIT licensed.
 *
 * @package EstatOS
 */

declare( strict_types = 1 );

namespace EstatOS\Support;

